I don't know if SATAP 4.2.5 has been posted before but check out the
contents of the bag of holding named Picnic Basket. (Ascension listing
is at the end)

This is my 5th ascension but first ascension post. I had wizard,
tourist, barbarian and priest under my belt when I saw Harold Hill's
SATAP web page. This inspired me to try one of my own. Of the many
listed 4.2.5 "Got a tin of every type of monster encountered (that
leaves a tinnable corpse)" tempted me most

To be honest I have been working on this for about a 6 months, trying a
mix of mostly monks and archeologists. I lost some very good characters
on the way, a 31st level rogue to a #q instead of a shift-s. I gave up
for a month or so after that debacle. A 24th level knight double teamed
to by two Arch liches after having his CoMR vaporised by a black dragon
which one of them had summoned. But I persevered. And eventually along
came Walter the Monk.

Learning from previous mistakes I found a =3DoFA early on, within the
first few levels, put it on and never took it off again. Similarly with
the "oR provided by Sokoban. The early game yielded a few wishes, a
lamp, a throne, a water demon. These provided the GoP's, the BoS and
the HoBrilliance.

As for challenges one not mentioned is that I never used the E word,
not even to protect my stashes. I'm not sure why I didn't get
vegtarianism. I don't recall eating anything untoward. I also refrained
from attacking anything with a weapon, though I did forget to unweild
the pick-axe on occasions which is why I failed this challenge. When I
did hit soemthing with the pick-axe I immediately unweilded it and
fought hand to hand. So in a way this was morally a succesful
challenge, but in a much more precise and Boulean sense it was failed.
I was not too upset by these set backs as the aim was the SATAP. I also
missed out on the never polymorphing as I spent some time as a rabid
rat. A year or two ago this would have freaked me out but now it just
makes for an interesting diversion until you turn back.

As for corpses, non of the uniques left a corpse. There was even a
portal to Creosus's vault but he didn't oblige. I used a mammoth to
batter to death various others, the Oracle, friendly priests, the Grand
Master but no one left a corpse.

With the ealry wishes and the ones from the castle, 10 in all,I got
fitted for armour and chose the PYEC over the Eye, I didn't want to
take off the "oR. Considering the SATAP I could probably have spent the
wishes better, but saying that I never found any other GoP's or
HoBrillaince, even after 150k turns. However, there are some corpses
which aren't left in the game but that can be wished for. All in all I
make it 240 different tinned corpses. I think it should be relatively
straight forward to extend this to 250, with a little more planning,
e=2Eg. choosing a character which will meet more types of humans on the
quest for instance.

Highlights;

-Queen bees, I used four cursed ?oGenocide to generate 18 of these
beauties before one left a corpse. Two also occured naturally but
didn't oblige either. After killing 12 I was seriously wondering if
these things were going to leave a corpse

-Collecting the last creature (werejackal). All the final creatures
were low level. My final 6 were werejackal, red mold, large kobold,
brown mold, queen bees and guard captain. Probably the last 40k turns
were spent after these last 6. I killed plenty of them, they just
wouldn't leave corpses. I had collected four ?oGenocide and polypiled
unihorns to get a MM to right three more and then waited for some
cursed water. A passing lich kindly cursed some for me and allowed me
to curse the scrolls. (I wanted to try to play to my religion so had to
get the water cursed the hard way). I'd had red mold before but my pet
mammoth ate it before I could tin it. My final cursed ?oGenocide was
used for werejackal. I was gutted to hear the "A cavernous voice booms
out ... No mortal it shall not be". I faced the prospect of traipsing
all the way back up to the top and another god knows how many 10's of
thousands of turns casting create monster. I had already killed 7
werejackals but no corpse. But what do you know, on the second level
going up, running between staircases I meet one head on. A quick karate
chop to the mussel, and hey presto creatures collected. Sweet.

I will say it was at this point I got very nervous. Everything was
ready to go and the anxiety of lossing the character to a stupid
mistake after all this time was quiet intense. This was heightened by
my poor AC (-17). I had lost all all my protection previously, #p
intead of #o during a sac fest. I fact I did it twice, lossing 10 pts
the first time and five the second. After the second time all I got was
spellbooks, no more protection.

-I had one more cursed ?oGenocide left, i was saving this for
salamanders. I'd met a few in Ghennom but no corpse. I had tried
reverse genocide earlier but was rewarded with "A cavernous voice booms
out ... No mortal it shall not be". I figured maybe the devteam would
allow it on the plane of fire. As they say TDTRDTOE. However, the
second salamnder I killed on fire leaves a corpse and there was no need
to use the scroll.

- The inner sanctum was interesting with an Arch Lich and Yeenoghu
double teaming me, along with everyone else. But in the end Yeenoghu
fell to a !oParalysis, as did so many of the unique badies during the
game, and the lich could be ignored, just keeping an eye on what was
being cursed and what creatures were gating in.

- I knew the riders left corpses so planned to collect them on the way
out. Something I wont be trying again in a hurry. Famine was first. One
thing I wasn't short of was /oDeath. I had lots, I even left some
behind. Famine went down first time, get the tins out. Oh bugger. He
resurects right next to me, next thing I know I am stunned and he is
doing about 70 points of damage per turn. Being weighted down with 240
cans iof food didn't seem like a good idea at this time. I forget if it
was 4 or 5 turns until I got things stabalised but I free fall from 430
to 50 Hp's. If I had met death first I would probably be drunk and very
bitter by now. But I turn it around and the rest, as they say, is
history

Comments are appreciated


